SCOPE CLAIMS — claims about the reader, or about people in general.
Same test, other direction: find the source sentence that makes this claim
about PEOPLE. If the source only says it about Nino's own system, the
caption must say it about his system. A reader who does the thing you said
nobody does will answer the premise instead of the idea.

